---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SM Global Accounting Services"
  description="How SM Global Accounting Services collects, uses and protects personal data when you visit this website or contact us."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated: 7 October 2026</p>

      <p class="placeholder-note" style="margin: var(--space-3) 0; max-width: none;">
        <strong>Draft for review.</strong> This policy has not yet been reviewed by a solicitor. Items
        in [square brackets] must be completed before the site goes live.
      </p>

      <div class="grid" style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: var(--space-3); margin-inline: auto;">
        <div>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This website is operated by {SITE.name} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;), a business
            registered in India: [legal entity name and registration type and number], [registered
            address]. We provide outsourced bookkeeping, statutory accounts, tax and related accounting
            support to accountancy practices, mainly in the UK. We are the controller of the personal
            data described in this policy. You can contact us at
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains how we handle personal data collected through this website, for
            example when you fill in the contact form. It does not cover how we handle client data
            while carrying out accounting work for a practice we are engaged by. That is governed
            separately by our engagement letter and data processing agreement with that practice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Details you give us directly: your name, practice name, email address, phone number (optional) and the content of your message.</li>
            <li>Standard technical data. Our website is hosted on GitHub Pages, which, like any web host, may process your IP address and browser details to deliver the pages to you. We do not add any tracking or analytics of our own.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>4. How we use it</h2>
          <p>We use the information you send us to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reply to your enquiry and arrange a consultation.</li>
            <li>Correspond with you about a possible or existing engagement.</li>
            <li>Meet our own legal and accounting obligations.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For people in the UK, our legal basis is our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries
            from prospective clients and, where an engagement follows, performing that contract. We do
            not use your details for marketing unless you ask us to.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>5. Where your data is processed</h2>
          <p>
            We are based in India, so your enquiry is received and processed in India. Our service
            providers (see section 7) may also process data in other countries. We only share what is
            needed to deliver the service, and we ask our providers to protect it. [Your adviser should
            confirm the safeguards to state here for UK and EU visitors before publishing.]
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            We keep enquiry details for as long as needed to respond to you and, if an engagement
            follows, for the length of that engagement plus [retention period] to meet our legal and
            accounting obligations. After that we delete them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>7. Sharing your data</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell personal data. The contact form is delivered by FormSubmit (formsubmit.co),
            a third-party form-delivery service. It receives what you submit and forwards it to our
            inbox. We also use email hosting [provider name] and GitHub Pages for hosting. We may share
            data with other providers who help us run this website or our business, under
            confidentiality obligations. We may also share data where the law requires it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>8. Cookies and tracking</h2>
          <p>
            This site does not set cookies and does not use analytics, advertising or tracking tools.
            If that changes, we will update this section and, where the law requires it, ask for your
            consent first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you are, you may have the right to access, correct or delete your
            personal data, to restrict or object to our use of it, and to withdraw consent where we rely
            on it. To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
            If you are in the UK, you can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office
            (ICO) at ico.org.uk. We also handle personal data in line with applicable Indian law,
            including the Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 as its provisions come into force.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top shows the current version.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
